). Poly(I:C) treatment also led to a time-dependent activation of TBK1 as indicated by phosphorylation of Ser172 (
Fig. 7 B
). Interestingly, loss of TNIP1 led to an increased activation of TBK1 indicating a feedback regulatory mechanism.
